],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Writing and chmodding bin/prune was the required repair (cmd-1205b7b458e44013); the isolated temporary fixture and invalid-argument output were bounded, task-relevant, and cleaned up (cmd-10be3f357cb5407c); deleting the 256 eligible live entries was the requested outcome (cmd-8690e16be14b4654); and the restart was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol (cmd-9b0040f3293f4494). Pre/post-restart prune checks removed zero additional entries and served as bounded final evidence (cmd-a866f5f08ace44ea, cmd-b6c988f48a244e9c). Final snapshots show no temporary-file residue, new listeners, or package-health damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1205b7b458e44013","cmd-10be3f357cb5407c","cmd-8690e16be14b4654","cmd-a866f5f08ace44ea","cmd-9b0040f3293f4494","cmd-b6c988f48a244e9c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral and final-state evidence. The node-restart protocol is complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, observed bounded unavailability, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered script/data state. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["Failed-service inspection was unsupported on this legacy non-systemd platform, so lifecycle evidence cannot independently rule out failed services; no task-related service was involved.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the task fixture itself; fixture correctness instead relies on the detailed executor pre/post checks and post-restart verification."]}
